# Verifying changes

Run `make check` (compiles the schema, lints, runs the headless tests) before
reporting work as done. Add a case to `tests/smoke.js` for any new logic in
`lib/`; it runs under plain `gjs` with a fixture config and an in-memory
GSettings backend, so it must stay free of side effects.

## You cannot restart GNOME Shell

The session is Wayland, so the shell cannot be restarted in place and
`gnome-extensions list` will not show a newly linked extension until the user
logs out and back in. Never claim the extension was loaded or enabled without
evidence. To exercise shell-side code, use `make nested` (GNOME 49+:
`gnome-shell --devkit --wayland`; requires `mutter-dev-bin` on Ubuntu), and tell the user when a logout is genuinely required.

`make logs` follows `gnome-shell` output for runtime errors.

## Testing mounts safely

The user has real rclone mounts in use. Never unmount, remount or otherwise
disturb a mount you did not create. To test the mount path, use a scratch mount
point and clean it up:

```bash
rclone mount --daemon <remote>: ~/mnt/scratch-test --read-only
rg -n 'scratch-test' /proc/self/mounts   # confirm it mounted
fusermount3 -uz ~/mnt/scratch-test       # lazy unmount; plain -u often gives EBUSY
```

Check `/proc/self/mounts` before and after to confirm pre-existing mounts are
untouched.

## Do not edit generated files

`schemas/gschemas.compiled` and `node_modules/` are build output and are ignored
by git.
